    {
      "id": "26040c14-135f-5a8a-beac-db776b9ffb6b",
      "name": "About",
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Processor: drains the event queue in batches\nEvery 30 s, at most `max_batches` batches of up to `batch_size` events of one type.\n\n`claim_batch()` takes the lease (one run at a time), then locks the oldest due events of one type. It returns\nnothing when another run holds the lease, the queue is empty, or Xero is paused, and each of those ends the run.\n\nA handler returns `{event_id, error}` per event. `finish_batch()` marks each done, retrying (backoff 30 s ... 1 h),\nor dead (after `max_attempts`, or at once for `PERMANENT:` errors). A handler failing as a whole fails every event\nin the batch; `XERO_RATE_LIMITED retry_after=N` instead pauses Xero work for N s without counting an attempt.\nDead events are announced on Telegram. If a run dies midway, its lease and locks expire after `lease_ttl`.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 760
      },
